Falsifies `capability::a_survey_shows_exactly_the_endpoints_own_children`.

The defect: `survey_includes` reports every supervised thread rather than only the
ones supervised *here*. This is what a `ps` written to be useful looks like before
anybody asks who is allowed to see what, and it is the confinement half of milestone
126's claim: with it, any process holding a rendezvous can enumerate every other
supervisor's children.

Expected to fail: the single `assert_eq!(survey_includes(fault_ep, invoked),
fault_ep == Some(invoked))`, which is the harness's only assertion, on any
`fault_ep` naming a rendezvous other than the invoked one.

The same defect also turns `the_view_and_the_reap_have_the_same_scope` red, and
that overlap is the point of recording both: the view's scope is not stated once,
it is stated as a predicate and again as an agreement with the reap, so a single
widening is caught twice. It is not caught by anything in the `reap_decision`
harnesses, which this patch leaves untouched.

diff --git a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
index d65bed7d..ffe0d92b 100644
--- a/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability/src/lib.rs
@@ -186,8 +186,8 @@ pub const fn reap_decision(fault_ep: Option<u64>, invoked_ep: u64, dead: bool) -
 /// (`sched::survey_supervised`). It is the predicate [`reap_decision`] authorizes with, so the
 /// threads a supervisor sees are the ones whose deaths reach it. Liveness is not an input: an
 /// uncollected corpse is still in the domain. See notes/capabilities/table.md ("Reap and survey").
-pub const fn survey_includes(fault_ep: Option<u64>, invoked_ep: u64) -> bool {
-    matches!(fault_ep, Some(ep) if ep == invoked_ep)
+pub const fn survey_includes(fault_ep: Option<u64>, _invoked_ep: u64) -> bool {
+    fault_ep.is_some()
 }
 
